  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the relationship between LCM and GCD:**\n   The relationship between the least common multiple (LCM) and the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute the given values:**\n   Given that the LCM is 3780, the GCD is 18, and one of the numbers \\(a = 180\\), we substitute these values into the formula:\n   \\[\n   3780 \\times 18 = 180 \\times b\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\(b\\):**\n   To find \\(b\\), we divide both sides of the equation by 180:\n   \\[\n   b = \\frac{3780 \\times 18}{180}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the value:**\n   \\[\n   b = 36\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{36}\n   \\]",
